{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he shall take from it.</b> From what is joined — so that a full tenth of an ephah in one vessel at the time of the fistful (Sifra)." "<b>When he takes the fistful.</b> That he not make a measure for the fistful (ibid.)." "<b>From the fine flour of the meal-offering and from its oil.</b> From here that he takes the fistful from the place where its oil is concentrated (Sotah 14)." "<b>The meal-offering.</b> That it not be mixed with another (Sifra)." "<b>And all the frankincense that is on the meal-offering, and shall burn it.</b> He gathers its frankincense after the fistful and burns it. And since this was specified only for one of the meal-offerings in Leviticus, it was necessary to repeat this passage, to include all the meal-offerings according to their law."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:26.718052543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}